# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Why this exists: main.cpp is stored CRLF upstream and LF here, and git
# compares blobs byte for byte during a merge. That one difference turned every
# sync with skypia into a whole-file conflict -- 6,065 lines the first time and
# 6,120 the second, none of it real. With the files normalised, `git merge
# -Xrenormalize` converts both sides before diffing and the conflict disappears.
#
# text=auto lets git detect binary files and leave them alone. Working copies
# still get CRLF on Windows via core.autocrlf; this governs what is STORED.
* text=auto

# Explicit, so a machine with core.autocrlf unset still checks these out the way
# Visual Studio expects.
*.cpp   text eol=crlf
*.h     text eol=crlf
*.ini   text eol=crlf

# Documentation is read on both platforms and by GitHub.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# LICENSE-GPL is deliberately NOT marked -text. It is an ordinary text file and
# is stored LF; marking it binary made `git add --renormalize` write the working
# copy's CRLF back into the blob, which is a 674-line diff that says nothing.
LICENSE-GPL text eol=lf
